# The frontend's environment. Copy to .env.local. Never commit the real file.
#
# ALL of these are optional. With none of them set, the frontend serves its own
# same-origin /api routes off web/data/opportunities.json -- the committed
# snapshot of 431 open calls -- and every screen works with no credentials.

# Point the browser at the standalone data service (api/, its own Vercel
# project). Set this and THIS deployment needs no Supabase credentials at all:
# they live only on the API project. The value is a public URL, which is why
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is correct here and nowhere else.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://your-api.vercel.app

# Only needed when NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE is NOT set, i.e. when this deployment
# reads Supabase itself through its own /api routes. SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY
# bypasses row-level security; it is read only by packages/server/src/source.ts,
# which carries `server-only`, so Next refuses to build if a client component
# ever imports it. Never add a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix to either of these.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=

# Rover, the agent chat (/rover). Optional: without it /api/rover answers 503
# and the screen says Rover is not switched on, while every other screen works
# exactly as before. It is the one feature here that costs money per use.
#
# This belongs on whichever deployment serves /api. If NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE is
# set, that is the API project, not this one — put the key there instead.
# Never prefix it NEXT_PUBLIC_: it is a secret, and the agent loop runs
# server-side precisely so it stays one.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# ROVER_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
